We are looking for a Project manager for our customer in Zaventem.
<br>
<br>We offer a unique opportunity for an experienced Project Manager to lead a transformative SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition program across 15 European countries, shaping a harmonized and future-ready ERP landscape.
<br>
<br>
<br>Main tasks and responsibilities:
<br>
<br>Lead the end-to-end implementation of SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition across 15 European countries;
<br>Manage the multinational rollout strategy, including governance, timelines, budget, risks, and dependencies;
<br>Coordinate cross-functional teams (Finance, Procurement, Supply Chain, Sales, Service, and IT);
<br>Align global template design and minimize local country requirements to ensure standardization;
<br>Manage system integrators, external partners, and SAP consultants;
<br>Ensure effective stakeholder communication at executive and country leadership levels;
<br>Oversee project planning, resource allocation, RAID management, and reporting;
<br>Support change management, training, and user adoption initiatives;
<br>Ensure compliance with European regulatory and localization requirements;
<br>Monitor project KPIs, milestones, and quality standards;
<br>Facilitate steering committee meetings and provide executive reporting.
Profile:
<br>
<br>5–10 years of SAP project management experience preferred;
<br>Proven track record in leading multinational SAP implementations across Europe;
<br>Strong experience with SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition implementations;
<br>Experience with large-scale multi-country ERP rollouts (10+ countries preferred);
<br>Solid understanding of SAP Public Cloud methodology and fit-to-standard approach;
<br>Experience working with international stakeholders and distributed teams;
<br>Strong leadership and stakeholder management capabilities.
<br>
<br>
<br>Professional skills:
<br>
<br>Excellent vendor and system integrator management skills;
<br>Strong knowledge of European localization, tax, and compliance requirements;
<br>Proven experience in risk management and governance;
<br>Excellent communication and executive presentation skills;
<br>Ability to manage complex projects and coordinate international teams;
<br>Experience with change management and user adoption strategies.

